{"seq":55,"at":"2026-10-23","kind":"reworded","target":{"type":"wording","id":"w13538"},"reason":"The card's claim that more than half of all rabbits live in North America has no population count behind it: it traces to an unsourced 1998 Texas Tech student page later copied into Wikipedia (since removed), while Australia alone holds 200–300 million feral rabbits. The question now asks what the widely repeated claim says; the card's words stay in cardText.","by":"provenance-research","sources":[{"url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20090804053012/http://courses.ttu.edu/thomas/classpet/1998/rabbit1/new_page_2.htm"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Rabbit&oldid=931362301"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rabbits_in_Australia"}],"changes":[{"field":"en","old":"On which continent do more than 50 percent of all the world's rabbits live?","new":"According to a widely repeated claim, on which continent do more than half of all the world's rabbits live?"},{"field":"de","old":"Auf welchem Kontinent leben mehr als 50 Prozent aller Kaninchen der Erde?","new":"Auf welchem Kontinent leben laut einer viel wiederholten Behauptung mehr als die Hälfte aller Kaninchen der Erde?"},{"field":"ru","old":"На каком континенте живёт больше 50 процентов всех кроликов Земли?","new":"На каком континенте, согласно часто повторяемому утверждению, живёт больше половины всех кроликов Земли?"},{"field":"cardText","new":"Auf welchem Kontinent leben mehr als 50 Prozent aller Kaninchen der Erde?"}],"hash":"3787b1858592","actor":{"kind":"agent","name":"provenance-research"},"run":"provenance-research-2026-10-23","chain":"a8e57690260ad950d165b56fecb8a13367fc76012c2390c40a388c5588e4f690"},
